From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_NX2_RANGE_PREFIX=1: reuse a contiguous range's page walk for shorter sizes

Off unless set. Port of zortos293/Lichii PR 580 (imports #478 by mstampfli), core hunk only; the
catch2 test and the templated Query are left out. VirtualRangeCache kept one size per address, so
Ocarina's alternating storage binding sizes replaced the entry and walked the page tables on every
size change. With the switch, a cached single segment answers any shorter size. The only caller,
BufferCache::ResolveMultiRangeStorage, returns early when the list has fewer than two segments, so
the oversized single segment is never used as a range. Unset: the exact-size match is unchanged.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/virtual_range_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/virtual_range_cache.h
index f4284d6..ed7ce9e 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/virtual_range_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/virtual_range_cache.h
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #pragma once
 
 #include <atomic>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <limits>
 #include <mutex>
 #include <optional>
@@ -44,6 +45,22 @@ public:
             it->second.gpu_addr == gpu_addr && it->second.size == size) {
             return &it->second.segments;
         }
+        // EDEN_NX2_RANGE_PREFIX=1 (Lichii #580 / #478): titles bind one address with several sizes
+        // (Ocarina of Time ~2,000 times a second, half of them over 1 MiB), and every size change
+        // replaced the entry and walked the page tables again. A prefix of a contiguous range is
+        // contiguous too, so a cached single segment answers any shorter size and the longest walk
+        // is kept. The returned segment may then cover more than was asked: the only caller
+        // (BufferCache::ResolveMultiRangeStorage) ignores lists with fewer than two segments.
+        // Lists of split ranges still match exactly.
+        static const bool range_prefix = [] {
+            const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_RANGE_PREFIX");
+            return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+        }();
+        if (range_prefix && it != entries.end() && it->second.as_id == as_id &&
+            it->second.gpu_addr == gpu_addr && it->second.segments.size() == 1 &&
+            size < it->second.size) {
+            return &it->second.segments;
+        }
         Entry entry{};
         entry.as_id = as_id;
         entry.gpu_addr = gpu_addr;
